+# Lemlandsvägen split at Strandnäs — 2026-11-11
+
+This resolves the deferred 40 m gap at the old Strandnäs crossing. The rural object `road:qgis:mariehamn:lemlandsvagen-2-100km3` was one 2,353 m line, first shown in 1985, because its eastern curve was realigned after 1978. It is now split at vertex 5 of way 45478307, just east of Södergård:
+
+| Object | Extent | First evidence | Metres |
+| --- | --- | --- | ---: |
+| `road:mariehamn:lemlandsvagen:strandnas-sodergard` (new) | Old crossing → Nabben → Kalmsta → Södergård | 1968 | 1,442.68 |
+| `road:mariehamn:lemlandsvagen:rokeri-approach` (new) | Rökerirondellen's eastern exit lane (way 43377949) | 1978 | 41.39 |
+| `road:qgis:mariehamn:lemlandsvagen-2-100km3` (kept) | Realigned curve east of Södergård | 1985 (unchanged) | 869 |
+| `road:qgis:mariehamn:lemlandsvagen-3-100km3` (kept) | Rökerirondellen's second eastern lane | 1978 (was 1985) | 30 |
+
+These 1,484 m are re-dated existing road, not new road length. They move the start of already-dated sections earlier and are reported separately from the 7,641.79 m of the second pass.
+
+**Evidence.** Centre lines were traced on the original-scan crops for each edition and measured against the modern line in EPSG:3874. The rule: points more than 40 m away are other red symbols, and each 150 m bin passes if its median deviation is at most 12 m.
+
+- **1968:** all bins 3.2–7.8 m.
+- **1978:** all bins 2.3–11.3 m. The 1978 sheet's registration offset is systematic.
+- **1985:** all bins 3.3–8.2 m.
+- **1995:** seven bins 5.0–6.9 m. Two bins fail numerically because the sheet prints a red-dashed cycle path and crossing streets beside the road. Both were checked visually on dedicated crops (`check1995a`, `check1995b`) and are recorded as visual checks; the compiler requires one for every failing bin.
+
+East of the split, row tracing shows 1968 and 1978 drifting 12–31 m south of today's curve from about 1,560 m along, while 1985 stays within 5–13 m and 1995 within 4–7 m. The 1968–1978 alignment matches modern cycle path 119232835 to within 0–7 m. The remainder therefore keeps its 1985 start, and the old curve is deferred with the other road-to-path conversions.
+
+**Identity and ownership.**
+- The kept object keeps its id, states, all 88 earlier evidence records (48 of them QGIS-review records) and its original geometry, recorded in `strandnasSplit.previousGeometryPeriods`. It gains a split record and 1968/1978 absence evidence for the current curve.
+- Its 51 whole and partial source ranges in the 2014/2021/2025/2026 OSM datasets are re-partitioned exactly. Way 45478307 is divided at the same physical point in every snapshot, using fractional vertex positions that the compiler recomputes. Every moved range is checked to lie on its new road.
+- The new objects also take the city-grid copies of their ways (2014–2026). Before the split those copies were unowned and drawn alongside the rural object; `lemlandsvagen-3` takes its own copy the same way.
+- In 1968 the old straight through-route at Strandnäs now meets Lemlandsvägen at the same node, and old Godbyvägen ends on it.
+
+**Files.**
+- `data/mariehamn-lemlandsvagen-split.json` is generated by `data/map-scan-cache/review/mariehamn-major-roads/lemlandsvagen/prepare.py`. That script is kept for audit and captures hashes, so do not rerun it blindly.
+- `scripts/mariehamn_lemlandsvagen_split.py` runs after the follow-up pass and validates everything before changing the catalogue.
+
+**Validation.** `lemlandsvagen/audit.py` rebuilds the catalogue with the split disabled; that baseline is identical to the pre-split catalogue. Against it, the split adds 2 objects and 3 prefixed geometries. Only the two Lemlandsvägen rural objects change, and only in their geometry reference, source links, appended evidence and split record. Earlier states, periods, evidence and links are preserved, and no other object, geometry or city stage changed.
+
+Tests: `tests/mariehamn-lemlandsvagen-split.test.cjs` and `tests/test_mariehamn_lemlandsvagen_split.py`. Three existing assertions were updated for the documented split:
+- the global identity count in `temporal-objects.test.cjs`;
+- in `qgis-roads.test.cjs`, ranges moved to the split sections, and the lane's 1978 start read from the object.
+
+**Publication.** Deployed 2026-11-11 as Cloudflare version `074f8450-e6bd-4e6b-ba4a-50420ecfdb4a`. The release was prepared from the live version (`e29d5e26…`, which already included two reported-building fixes) plus only the split: the catalogue, `assets/mariehamn-lemlandsvagen-split.json`, the loader card in `index.html`, and cache stamps in `temporal-objects.js` and `object.html`. Other unpublished workspace changes were left out. The live files were checked byte for byte against the release; see `lemlandsvagen/deployment.json`.
